{"t":27374,"dir":"in","frame":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","type":"notification","factoryApiVersion":"1.0.0","factoryProtocolVersion":"1.260.0","method":"droid.session_notification","params":{"sessionId":"<session-id>","notification":{"type":"create_message","message":{"id":"<id-4>","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. The ocean covers about 71% of Earth’s surface.  \n2. Most of Earth’s water is in the ocean.  \n3. The ocean helps regulate global climate.  \n4. Seawater is salty because of dissolved minerals.  \n5. The Pacific Ocean is the largest ocean.  \n6. The Atlantic Ocean is the second largest ocean.  \n7. The Indian Ocean is warm in many regions.  \n8. The Southern Ocean surrounds Antarctica.  \n9. The Arctic Ocean is the smallest ocean.  \n10. Ocean currents move heat around the planet.  \n11. Waves are mainly driven by wind.  \n12. Tides are caused by the Moon and Sun.  \n13. The deep ocean is very cold.  \n14. Sunlight only reaches the upper ocean layers.  \n15. The twilight zone has little light.  \n16. The deepest part of the ocean is the Mariana Trench.  \n17. Many ocean species are still undiscovered.  \n18. Coral reefs are rich marine ecosystems.  \n19. Phytoplankton produce a large share of Earth’s oxygen.  \n20. The ocean absorbs carbon dioxide from the air.  \n21. Marine snow carries food to deep-sea life.  \n22. Some whales migrate thousands of miles.  \n23. Dolphins are highly intelligent marine mammals.  \n24. Sharks have existed for hundreds of millions of years.  \n25. Octopuses are known for problem-solving.  \n26. Sea turtles can travel across whole ocean basins.  \n27. The ocean floor has mountains and valleys.  \n28. Mid-ocean ridges form new seafloor.  \n29. Hydrothermal vents support unusual life forms.  \n30. The ocean is connected by one global system.  \n31. Saltwater freezes at a lower temperature than fresh water.  \n32. Marine ecosystems support many human economies.  \n33. Fishing is an important ocean-based industry.  \n34. Oceans influence weather patterns on land.  \n35. Large storms can strengthen over warm water.  \n36. Plastic pollution is a major ocean problem.  \n37. Overfishing can reduce fish populations.  \n38. Rising sea levels threaten coastal areas.  \n39. The ocean makes up most of the biosphere’s habitable volume.  \n40. Exploring the ocean is still difficult and ongoing."}],"createdAt":1791848662642,"updatedAt":1791848662642,"modelId":"gpt-5.4-mini","apiProvider":"openai","reasoningEffort":"low","openaiMessageId":"msg_005cf7e7a420163f016acd70d3067887d0836bd7e5db5e4d2e","openaiPhase":"final_answer","parentId":"<id-3>","seq":8}}}}}
